  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nAmount (A₁) = ₹1060\n\nTime (t₁) = 2.5 years\n\nAmount (A₂) = ₹1000\n\nTime (t₂) = 1 year\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nSimple Interest (SI) = P × r × t / 100\n\nA = P + SI\n\n**Calculations:**\n\nFrom A₂:\n\n1000 = P + P × r × 1 / 100\n\n⇒ 1000 = P(1 + r / 100)\n\nFrom A₁:\n\n1060 = P + P × r × 2.5 / 100\n\n⇒ 1060 = P(1 + 2.5r / 100)\n\nNow, we have two equations:\n\n1) 1000 = P(1 + r / 100)\n\n2) 1060 = P(1 + 2.5r / 100)\n\nDividing equation 2 by equation 1:\n\n⇒ 1060 / 1000 = (P(1 + 2.5r / 100)) / (P(1 + r / 100))\n\n⇒ 1.06 = (1 + 2.5r / 100) / (1 + r / 100)\n\n⇒ 1.06(1 + r / 100) = 1 + 2.5r / 100\n\n⇒ 1.06 + 1.06r / 100 = 1 + 2.5r / 100\n\n⇒ 1.06 - 1 = 2.5r / 100 - 1.06r / 100\n\n⇒ 0.06 = 1.44r / 100\n\n⇒ 0.06 × 100 = 1.44r\n\n⇒ 6 = 1.44r\n\n⇒ r = 6 / 1.44\n\n⇒ r ≈ 4.17%\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option (2).**\n\n6b",
